fof_version: '1.0'
type: enemy
id: waiting_one
name: A Waiting One
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 1.0.0
enemy:
  # v0.3: Named, durability 4, attack +2, rating 9.
  level: 3
  role: standard
  armor: 0
  morale: 12
  weapon: The tools of its trade
  wants: The work done properly, and then done again.
  special: THE TASK — the MM knows the job it is doing. A character who spends their action
    genuinely advancing that job is not a target this exchange, and it works around them.
    Anyone who damages the work is its target from then on, and every hit it lands on them
    is a hard hit.
  when_bloodied: It turns its back and goes back to the job. From here it attacks only someone
    who damages the work or stands between it and the job.
  tells: It is finishing something that was finished before any of you were born. It has not
    looked up.
  breaks: Never breaks. It stops when the task is finished, and only then. At 0 HP it simply
    cannot go on, which is not the same thing, and the fiction should say so.
  twists:
  - The job takes ten minutes with a second pair of hands.
  - The thing the party came for is part of the work, and taking it is damaging the work.
  - The job needs a material that no longer exists.
  - Someone has been leaving materials at the door for forty years and has never once gone
    in.
  - Two Waiting Ones are doing the same job, and each has been undoing the other's work.
  - The job went wrong the day they died, and it will never come out right until someone finds
    out why.
  nastier: An Unfinished runs this site, and this one has been reassigned.
  description: >-
    Someone at work. The hands move, the tools are real, and the job is being done properly.
    It is only when you have watched for a while that you notice the job was finished a long
    time ago, and is being done again.
  notes: >-
    Level 3 standard: no overrides. Fearless (morale 12): nothing but a finished task stops
    it.


    Occupied. Violence is an interruption, and it is treated as one. It never attacks first,
    and never attacks anyone who is helping. A party that finishes the job is not opposed
    again.


    Appears: where people died mid-task, one to four, each on its own job.
  reskin_of: null
